    "register": "light",
    "notes": "Segment 4: Search Party UAE video fUrNOVjWUVM, 00:00-00:10. NO REFERENCE FRAMES were available (yt-dlp is not installed and the network is off), so nothing here is measured from the video. Built from tests/segments/seg4.json (Sudan and Darfur framing, El Fasher marker, RSF encirclement, El Fasher and RSF labels, one travel-land-hold camera beat) and the Harris tokens in src/map/tokens.json. Timing is authored, not measured: open framing held to f6 then still, SUDAN label f24, travel f67-f115, camera lands f115 (0.2 s before the event), event f120 (Sudan flood), ring draw f125-f161, RSF badge f135, EL FASHER label f145, camera still from f115 to f239 (more than 1.2 s after the last label). The ring is a schematic circle (radius 1.25 degrees) around El Fasher, not the real siege perimeter. Label font is the fixture Liberation Sans Bold; Montserrat Bold is not in assets/fonts, so type does not match the token spec. Palette is the light register from tokens.json, not a measured palette. Cycle 2 fix (coordinator, Nov 7): fasher camera zoom lowered 4.4 to 3.4 after reading the draft stills: at 4.4 the Sudan flood filled the whole frame, the SUDAN pill was pushed to the top-right edge, and no neighbour or sea context stayed in shot. At 3.4 Sudan plus a neighbour margin and the Red Sea edge stay in frame. Cycle 2 fix 2: ring radius 1.25 deg to 2.0 deg after reading v2 stills: at zoom 3.4 the 1.25 deg ring (about 160 px wide) was smaller than the EL FASHER pill (about 300 px), so the label dwarfed the feature it named. A 2.0 deg ring (about 260 px wide) balances the 48 px label and still sits inside Darfur."
  },
